# Read by sddm's daemon before it starts a greeter, not by the theme.
#
# **`QtVersion=6` is load-bearing and its absence fails quietly.**  sddm defaults it
# to 5 (`src/common/ThemeMetadata.cpp`) and then looks for an unsuffixed
# `bin/sddm-greeter`, which this sddm does not ship — it only has
# `sddm-greeter-qt6`.  The daemon then logs "requires missing .../sddm-greeter. Using
# fallback theme." and shows breeze instead, so the symptom is "my theme did not
# appear" with a working greeter and nothing on screen to say why.  Measured
# 2026-10-31: the first deploy of this theme did exactly that.
[SddmGreeterTheme]
Name=Leigh Hackspace Halloween
Description=A black Pi Room login screen that shows a random scare after a minute of silence.
Type=sddm-theme
Author=Leigh Hackspace
Copyright=Leigh Hackspace
License=MIT
Version=0.1
MainScript=Main.qml
ConfigFile=theme.conf
Theme-API=2.0
QtVersion=6
Theme-Id=leighhack-halloween
